PATCH 473: the eight remaining base-lost per-object UPDATE methods of the c0e5 dispatch table, plus the
bearing/pitch helper bbc6 and 054c's BX lane (board:0007 base-loss sweep / board:0012 self-play).

With patch 462 the object SPAWN core is correct, so the c0e5 -0x1bac table now really dispatches the
CHILD/PROJECTILE types; a table scan showed eight entries whose bodies still deref'd the DI near offset as
a host pointer (SEGV in 9b11 on the first 9caa child).  Rebuilt 1:1 from asm (each cited in its comment):
  9b11 (0x11 smoke child), 9bc6 (0x12), 9c4f (0x15 muzzle flash), 9e2b (0x05/0x06 ground vehicle),
  b481 (0x16 demolition charge), b808 (0x0e guided missile), b918 (0x0f rocket) with its CS-table state
  handlers b945 (boost) / b998 (homing), and 9d49 (0x18 smoke cloud, via 9b56).
Also: bbc6 (the target bearing/pitch: rebased, publishes BX) and 054c (0578's twin: 077e now gets 08e8's
range lanes from DAT_1000_c458/c45a instead of a dead input, and its result -- the PITCH -- is published as
g_fist_054c_bx, which every projectile stores into [obj+0x1e]/[obj+0x1f]).  Widths are asm-exact
([di+0xc]/[di+0x1a]/[di+0x1b]/[di+0x23] are WORD, not the 32-bit Ghidra typed), and the dropped register
lanes (0459's dx/cx, 03a9's dx, e1a6's sign, bb1b's CF, ba33's SI) are threaded.  b945/b998 take DI as
arg0 so b918's `call word[CS:0xb93f + state]` dispatch works through fist_icall_near.
